<!-- Use this page type — the HIGHEST-VALUE type — for any non-trivial choice made with
     the user that passes the write test: what was decided, the context that forced the choice, the alternatives
     weighed, and WHY this one won. This is the knowledge that most reliably survives
     context compaction and onboards the next session. Code shows WHAT; decisions show WHY.
     File a decision page whenever a real trade-off was made, an approach was rejected,
     or a constraint was agreed upon. One page per decision. Write test first: if the work
     order already records the why, there is no page. A decision is never rewritten; a reversal
     is a new page and the old one gets `status: superseded` + `superseded_by`. -->

